    "event": "Rip Current Statement",
    "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
    "senderName": "NWS Tiyan GU",
    "headline": "Rip Current Statement issued October 31 at 4:54AM ChST until October 31 at 4:00PM ChST by NWS Tiyan GU",
    "description": "* WHAT...Large breaking waves of 9 to 12 feet and dangerous rip\ncurrents expected.\n\n* WHERE...West and north facing reefs of Guam, Rota, Tinian and\nSaipan.\n\n* WHEN...Until 4 PM ChST this afternoon.\n\n* IMPACTS...Dangerous swimming and surfing conditions and\nlocalized beach erosion. Rip currents can sweep even the best\nswimmers away from shore into deeper water.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...As TY In-fa moves away from the far northern\nCNMI, the large, long-period northwest to north swell emanating\nfrom In-fa will maintain hazardous surf along north and west\nfacing reefs. Seas have begun to slowly subside and have gradually\nturned northwest, ending hazardous surf along east facing reefs and\nbeginning hazardous surf along west facing reefs. Surf will remain\nhazardous through this afternoon. These surf conditions will\nmaintain a high risk of dangerous rip currents. Although surf is\nnow below hazardous levels along east facing reefs, the rip current\nrisk will remain high.",
    "instruction": "Inexperienced swimmers should remain out of the water due to\ndangerous surf conditions.\n\nRip currents will be life threatening. If caught in a rip current,\nrelax and float. Don't swim against the current. If able, swim in a\ndirection following the shoreline. If unable to escape, face the\nshore and call or wave for help.",
    "response": "Avoid",
    "note": null,
